Q: Static Class in Java A: <p>A <code>static class</code> is only legal for a <strong>nested class</strong>, not a top-level class.</p>
<p>If your mentioned Schildt's example appears inside another class, then this for example is valid:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>class Company {
    static class RegularEmployee implements Employee {}
}
</code></pre>
<p>But at the top level, <code>static</code> is not allowed, so your IDE just reports you the compile-time error. Nested classes, interfaces, enums or records can be declared static.</p>
<p>If you share more information about the text in the book we could maybe point out where the misunderstanding happened.</p>
